id: interface/decision-sufficiency-view-v0.1
title: "Decision Sufficiency View contract v0.1"
kind: interface-contract
record_shape: header
status: draft
version: 0.1.0
updated: 2026-09-30
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Codex, defining the experimental Decision Sufficiency View on behalf of the maintainer"

purpose: >
  Describe a Dave-only, private interface intention for inspecting one
  experimental Decision Sufficiency receipt as Coarse, Witness, and Refined
  views of the same attributed synthetic computation.

provisioning:
  principal_ref: principal:dave
  audience: [principal:dave]
  public_exposure: false
  proposed_route: /dave/research/decision-sufficiency
  app_repository: yawn-ai/yawn.bot
  status: intention_only
  activation_requires:
    - explicit_principal_provisioning
    - generated_receipt_artifact
    - receipt_schema_validation
  rule: >
    This contract names a private intended surface. It does not itself deploy
    the proposed app route, read private Dave data, create a record, or imply
    that a browser surface has been verified.

primary_object:
  kind: decision-sufficiency-receipt
  source_artifact: fixtures/decision-sufficiency.v0.1.json
  source_pointer: receipts/0
  receipt_schema: schemas/decision-sufficiency-receipt.v0.1.schema.json
  generator: scripts/generate-decision-sufficiency-v0.1.mjs
  rule: >
    Coarse, Witness, and Refined remain projections of one receipt and its
    generated artifact. Changing the selected View never creates a second
    decision, a new approval, or a new authority record.

views:
  coarse:
    shows:
      - query_text
      - visible_fields
      - visible_fiber_value
      - recorded_decision_values
      - recorded_decision_state
      - enforcement_disposition
    rule: >
      Show that the coarse projection is unresolved when its one visible fiber
      contains both recorded reference decisions. The block is a refusal to
      claim sufficiency, not an action gate on a live operation.
  witness:
    shows:
      - ambiguity_witness_state_pair
      - fields_that_differ
      - each_recorded_reference_decision
      - source_and_binding_digests
    rule: >
      The witness is generated finite-state evidence that the coarse projection
      loses a relevant distinction. It is not evidence from a person, a claim
      about a real-world relationship, or a disclosure grant.
  refined:
    shows:
      - all_minimum_refinements
      - canonical_refinement
      - conditional_necessity_witnesses
      - refined_fiber_summary
    rule: >
      A canonical refinement is a deterministic display representative. Tied
      minimum refinements remain visible, and a necessity witness is scoped to
      the selected minimum and declared synthetic state space.

coordinates:
  receipt_time: recorded_artifact
  scope: synthetic_finite_state_space
  aperture: [coarse, witness, refined]
  global_resolution_boundary: >
    Coarse, Witness, and Refined are semantic apertures over one receipt. They
    are distinct from the application-wide glance, standard, and deep display
    resolution controls.
  selection_rule: "All three apertures use the same receipt ID and binding set."
  stale_behavior: >
    When a current binding differs, show stale and block. Preserve the historic
    receipt without presenting it as current or regenerating its past result.

evidence:
  source: generated_fixture_and_independent_replay_tests
  human_trial: not_run
  claim_boundary: >
    The evidence is the generator's exact finite partition, the persisted
    receipt, and validation. It does not claim usability evidence, a human
    trial, a live decision, or a deployed interface outcome.

app_runtime:
  repository: yawn-ai/yawn.bot
  verification_status: pending_app_repo_verification
  rule: >
    The protocol fixture and schema are verified locally. App implementation,
    provisioning behavior, and browser rendering require separate verification
    in the app repository and are not claimed by this record.

authority:
  mutationAuthorized: false
  persistenceAuthorized: false
  modelCallAuthorized: false
  externalEffectsAuthorized: false
  receiptGrantsAuthority: false
  projectionGrantsAuthority: false
  refinementGrantsDisclosure: false
  rule: >
    Opening, zooming, comparing, or replaying the View cannot authenticate an
    approval basis, check revocation, grant permission, disclose data, invoke a
    model, or trigger an external effect.

limitations:
  - "Approval basis is tested for presence in the reused gate, not independently verified for legitimacy or revocation."
  - "The evaluator binding covers the gate source, adapter/generator source, and synthetic source fixture; it is not a live-environment attestation."
  - "Minimum cardinality is relative to the declared raw candidate fields and can change if the candidate universe changes."
  - "A receipt digest detects ordinary mutation only when recomputed; it is not a signature or proof of truth."

proof:
  source:
    - fixtures/decision-sufficiency.v0.1.json
    - schemas/decision-sufficiency-receipt.v0.1.schema.json
    - fixtures/decision-sufficiency-receipt.v0.1.invalid.json
    - tests/decision-sufficiency-v0.1.test.mjs
  acceptance:
    - "The generated receipt validates and each declared invalid mutation is rejected."
    - "Coarse, Witness, and Refined all identify the same receipt and binding set."
    - "The View reports generated evidence and does not claim a human trial or live effect."
    - "Every current/stale distinction preserves the historical receipt and blocks stale use."
  status: schema_and_finite_fixture_verified
